%N A117688 Cubes for which the sum of the digits is a square.
%C A117688 If k is a term then so is 1000*k. - _Robert Israel_, Aug 10 2026
%D A117688 Elena Deza and Michel Marie Deza, Figurate numbers, World Scientific Publishing (2012), page 422.
%H A117688 Robert Israel, <a href="/A117688/b117688.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A117688 216 is in the sequence because it is a cube and the sum of its digits 2+1+6=9 is a square.
%p A117688 filter:= k -> issqr(convert(convert(k,base,10),`+`)):
%p A117688 select(filter, [seq(i^3,i=0..1000)]); # _Robert Israel_, Aug 10 2026
%t A117688 Select[Range[0,300]^3,IntegerQ[Sqrt[Total[IntegerDigits[#]]]]&] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Mar 29 2012 *)
